    <statement><p>Calculate the flux of the vector field
<m>\vec{F}(x,y,z) = (4 x + 4) \vec{i}</m> 
through a disk of radius <m>4</m>
centered at the origin in the yz-plane, 
oriented in the negative x-direction.</p>
<p>Flux = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <hint/>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-\pi \cdot 4\cdot 4^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
